## 🔴 Critical / High Severity

### 1. Unauthenticated PII Exposure (`/users` endpoint)
**OWASP A01 – Broken Access Control | A02 – Cryptographic Failures**

The `/users` route returns user data (names and emails) to **any caller with no authentication, no authorization, and no rate limiting**. Email addresses are PII under GDPR, CCPA, and most privacy frameworks.

```js
// ❌ CURRENT — fully open, no auth
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    ...
  ]);
});
```

**✅ Recommendation — Add authentication middleware:**
```js
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

function requireAuth(req, res, next) {
  const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];
  const token = authHeader?.startsWith('Bearer ') ? authHeader.slice(7) : null;

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Missing authentication token' });
  }

  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    next();
  } catch {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid or expired token' });
  }
}

// ✅ Protected route
app.get('/users', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  // Also: fetch from DB, don't hardcode data
  res.json(users);
});
```

